"""Render reviewed set-screw selections without inventory claims."""
import json
DATA=json.loads((W/'scripts/mil-spec-set-screw-data.json').read_text())
for root,data in DATA.items():
 file='Reference-'+root+'.html';dog=data['point']=='Half-dog';cup=data['point']=='Cup'
 identity=root+' identifies '+data['material']+' hex-socket '+data['point'].lower()+'-point set screws with '+data['thread_series']+' threads and a '+data['finish'].lower()+' finish in the reviewed issue. This table covers '+data['scope']+'.'
 if root=='MS51031':identity+=' These selected dash numbers identify self-locking screws; plain screws use different dash numbers.'
 elif root!='MS51047':identity+=' The selected rows identify plain screws without a self-locking element.'
 rows=[]
 fields=['part','thread','length','length_tolerance','socket_nominal','point_diameter_limits']+(['point_length_limits']if dog else[])
 for r in data['rows']:
  rows.append([h(r[f])for f in fields]+[h(data['configuration'])]+['<a href="Quote.html?reference='+file+'&amp;part='+h(r['part'])+'">Quote '+h(r['part'])+' →</a>'])
 heads=['Part number','Thread','Length per drawing (in)','Length tolerance (in)','Socket AF nominal J (in)',('Dog diameter limits P (in)'if dog else('Plain cup diameter limits C (in)'if cup else'Flat point diameter limits C (in)'))]+(['Dog length limits Q (in)']if dog else[])+['Configuration','Request pricing']
 body='<p>Reference selections for purchasing identification and quotation. Webson confirms availability by inquiry; these rows do not indicate stocked inventory. Configuration shown: '+data['configuration'].lower()+'.</p>'+filtered(heads,rows,root+' reference set screw dimensions')
 body+='<p>All dimensions are in inches. Length preserves printed decimal values such as 0.188 and 0.312; the adjacent ± value is the drawing’s length tolerance. Point values are minimum–maximum limits. J is the drawing’s nominal socket width across flats, not a measured acceptance range.</p>'
 if cup:body+='<p>C applies to the plain cup profile. The reviewed drawing also permits other cup forms with separate C1, C2 and S requirements. The series and these C limits alone do not identify a knurled, hexagon, small-cup or other optional point form; include any specified point-form requirement in the inquiry.</p>'
 if dog:measure='<p>L is overall screw length from the socket end to the end of the projecting dog. Q is only the dog projection, and P is its diameter. The dog is included in L; do not add Q to the listed length or treat L as the threaded engagement length.</p><p>The reduced cylindrical point must match the receiving feature specified by the assembly drawing. A thread and length match does not establish that a cup or flat point can replace a half-dog point.</p>'
 elif cup:measure='<p>L is overall screw length from the socket end to the point end. C in the table identifies the diameter of the plain cup profile. The recessed point and socket recess are different features; socket size is listed separately as J.</p><p>A cup-point designation does not establish a particular optional knurl, cup form, tightening torque or mating-surface suitability. Follow the assembly drawing for those requirements.</p>'
 else:measure='<p>L is overall screw length from the socket end to the flat point. C is the flat point diameter; J is nominal socket width across flats. The point and socket dimensions describe different ends of the screw.</p><p>The flat contact end differs from a recessed cup point and a projecting half-dog point. Confirm the required contact geometry before comparing replacement sizes.</p>'
 if root=='MS51031':config='<p>The selected MS51031B rows are self-locking references in the 10-32 and 1/4-28 columns. Locking is encoded by the table’s dash number, not by adding an L suffix. For example, MS51031-107 is a self-locking 10-32 screw with a 0.500-inch length. The reviewed drawing’s asterisked inactive-for-new-design selections are outside this table.</p><p>The locking element, effective locking area and torque provisions remain subject to the governing procurement issue and assembly requirements. This selected table does not supply a tightening torque.</p>'
 elif root=='MS51047':config='<p>MS51047-47 identifies a 1/4-28 half-dog screw with 0.500-inch overall length. Its dog projection Q is 0.059–0.067 inch, included in that overall length.</p><p>The reviewed MS51047B issue marks this family inactive for new design after 29 December 1972. These rows support identification of existing drawing callouts. They are not a recommendation for new designs or an automatic conversion to another standard.</p>'
 elif root=='MS51965':config='<p>MS51965-55 identifies a plain 1/4-20 flat-point screw with a 0.500-inch length. MS51965-79 identifies a plain 3/8-16 screw with the same length. The selected table contains all 52 plain entries in the reviewed Table I; separate self-locking dash numbers are outside this selection.</p><p>The reviewed alloy-steel requirement specifies Rockwell C45–53 and cadmium plating. A shared thread or length does not make the cup-point MS51963 or stainless fine-thread MS51031 an approved alternate.</p>'
 elif root=='MS51023':config='<p>MS51023-52 identifies a plain 10-32 cup-point screw with 0.500-inch length. MS51023-64 is a plain 1/4-28 screw with the same length. The reviewed issue also has self-locking dash-number columns; those configurations are outside this selected plain-screw table. Do not add a locking suffix or copy a dash number from another family.</p>'
 else:config='<p>MS51963-51 identifies a plain 10-24 cup-point screw with 0.500-inch length. MS51963-67 is a plain 1/4-20 screw with the same length. The reviewed issue also lists separate self-locking dash numbers for some sizes; those are outside this selected table.</p><p>The reviewed alloy steel requirement specifies Rockwell C45–53 and cadmium plating. A stainless screw with a similar nominal size has a different material and finish requirement.</p>'
 compare=[['<a href="Reference-MS51021.html">MS51021</a>','Cup','UNC-3A','Passivated stainless steel','Selected plain sizes']]
 for other,d in DATA.items():compare.append(['<a href="Reference-'+other+'.html">'+other+'</a>',d['point'],d['thread_series'],d['finish']+' '+d['material'],d['configuration']+' selections'])
 related=filtered(['Series','Point','Thread series','Material and finish','Table configuration'],compare,'Set screw family selection')+'<p>Compare the point, thread, material, finish and locking configuration together. These family comparisons do not establish an approved substitution.</p>'+chips([('Set-screw family directory','Reference-Family-set-screws.html'),('MS51021 coarse stainless cup points','Reference-MS51021.html')])
 guide(file,root+' Set Screws | Thread Sizes & Point Dimensions',root+' '+data['point'].lower()+'-point set screws.','Find '+root+' thread sizes, screw lengths, nominal socket sizes and point dimensions. Filter selected references and request a quote.',[
 ('Identify the point, thread and configuration','<p>'+identity+'</p>','PART IDENTIFICATION'),
 (root+' part-number and dimension table',body,'REFERENCE SIZES'),
 ('Measure length and point geometry',measure,'MEASUREMENT GUIDE'),
 ('Read the dash number and locking requirement',config,'ORDERING DETAILS'),
 ('Compare related set-screw families',related,'FAMILY COMPARISON'),
 ('Match the governing drawing issue','<p>Dimensions summarize '+h(data['reviewed_issue'])+'. These are selected historical references for purchasing identification. The issue required by your drawing controls full geometry, thread requirements, material, finish, locking provisions and inspection. No automatic successor or part-number substitution is implied.</p>','DRAWING REQUIREMENTS')])
